{"id":198218557,"iid":8510,"project_id":34675721,"title":"Skill discovery reports false collision when `.agents` is a symlink to a subdirectory","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen `.agents` at the repository root is a **symlink** pointing to a subdirectory within the same repository (e.g. `agent-capabilities/.agents`), `glab duo cli` reports a skill name collision at startup and skips the duplicate — even though both paths resolve to the exact same files on disk.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Have a repository where `.agents` is a symlink:\n   ```\n   \u003crepo-root\u003e/\n   ├── .agents -\u003e agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.agents   # symlink\n   ├── agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/\n   │   └── .agents/\n   │       └── skills/\n   │           └── review-ticket-work/\n   │               └── SKILL.md\n   └── .git/\n   ```\n2. Run `glab duo cli` from that repository root.\n\n## Observed behaviour\n\n```\n[Skill conflicts]\n  \"review-ticket-work\" collision:\n    ✓ .agents/skills/review-ticket-work/SKILL.md (workspace)\n    ✗ agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.agents/skills/review-ticket-work/SKILL.md (workspace, skipped)\n```\n\nThe skill is loaded correctly (the `✓` path wins), but every skill in the symlinked directory produces a spurious collision warning.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nNo collision warning. When two candidate paths resolve to the same inode (or the same real path via `filepath.EvalSymlinks`), the discovery walker should treat them as one skill, not two.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`defaultCandidateLocations()` in `internal/commands/skills/installed/installed.go` derives the single project-scope location from `git.ToplevelDir()`:\n\n```go\nfunc defaultCandidateLocations() []location {\n    var out []location\n    if root, err := git.ToplevelDir(); err == nil {\n        out = append(out, location{filepath.Join(root, skillsRelDir), ScopeProject})\n    }\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n`skillsRelDir` is `.agents/skills`. When `.agents` is a symlink, `os.ReadDir(\".agents/skills\")` resolves through it and returns the skill directories. However, the real target path (`agent-capabilities-for-gitlab-support/.agents/skills/`) is also a subdirectory of the same git root and is therefore also reachable by a directory walk of the workspace — which is how `glab duo cli`'s collision detection finds it a second time.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nBefore registering a discovered skill path, resolve it to its real path with `filepath.EvalSymlinks` and deduplicate by real path. Two entries that resolve to the same real path should be treated as one, with the first (symlink) path taking precedence.\n\nAlternatively, `readSkillDirs` could skip entries where `os.Lstat` reveals the entry is itself a symlink whose target is already registered.\n\n## Environment\n\n- `glab duo cli` (latest)\n- macOS (Apple Silicon), Podman-based container workspace\n- Repository: [`gitlab-com/support/toolbox/duo-workspace`](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-com/support/toolbox/duo-workspace), which uses this symlink pattern intentionally to expose a git submodule's skills to the Duo CLI","state":"closed","created_at":"2026-08-21T21:29:05.304Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T06:29:47.560Z","closed_at":"2026-08-26T18:26:37.574Z","closed_by":{"id":2935693,"username":"phikai","public_email":"karmstrong@gitlab.com","name":"Kai Armstrong","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/2935693/avatar.png?v=1792535022","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/phikai"},"labels":["automation:ml","automation:quick-win","automation:quick-win-judged","backend","bug::functional","category:gitlab cli","devops::ai coding","group::code review","quick win","section::ai","type::bug"],"milestone":null,"assignees":[],"author":{"id":5537005,"username":"cleveland","public_email":"","name":"Cleveland Bledsoe Jr","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/5537005/avatar.png?v=1792525248","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/cleveland"},"type":"ISSUE","assignee":null,"user_notes_count":3,"merge_requests_count":0,"upvotes":0,"downvotes":0,"start_date":null,"due_date":null,"confidential":false,"discussion_locked":null,"issue_type":"issue","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/work_items/8510","time_stats":{"time_estimate":0,"total_time_spent":0,"human_time_estimate":null,"human_total_time_spent":null},"task_completion_status":{"count":0,"completed_count":0},"weight":null,"blocking_issues_count":0,"has_tasks":true,"task_status":"0 of 0 checklist items completed","_links":{"self":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/34675721/issues/8510","notes":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/34675721/issues/8510/notes","award_emoji":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/34675721/issues/8510/award_emoji","project":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/34675721","closed_as_duplicate_of":null},"references":{"short":"#8510","relative":"#8510","full":"gitlab-org/cli#8510"},"severity":"UNKNOWN","subscribed":false,"moved_to_id":199237411,"imported":false,"imported_from":"none","service_desk_reply_to":null,"epic_iid":null,"epic":null,"iteration":null,"health_status":null}